# Production-grade product (not a practice app)

Serveo will be deployed. Treat every change as shipping toward production.

## Non-negotiables

- Prefer patterns that survive swapping localStorage for a real API + database.
- Shape data access like backend contracts: paginated lists (`items`, `nextCursor`, `hasMore`, `total`), typed IDs, explicit status enums.
- Do not load unbounded lists into the DOM. Use pagination / infinite scroll / virtualization for catalogs and inboxes.
- Keep UI components dumb; put query/pagination/filter logic in hooks or `lib/` so the data source can move to fetch/API later.
- Avoid throwaway prototype shortcuts that force large rewrites at backend integration (duplicate sources of truth, hard-coded full arrays in pages, client-only IDs that cannot map to DB rows).
- Optimize for deploy: local assets under `public/` when practical, `next/image`, no unnecessary client JS, accessible loading/empty/error states.
- Prefer incremental loading and skeletons over flashing full catalogs.
- When unsure, choose the option that needs the fewest changes after auth, Postgres, and real APIs land.
